# Build artifacts: Rust's target dir lives outside the repo (see the README),
# and the Node sidecar is a ~93 MB copy of the local node binary that belongs on
# nobody's disk - on every platform, not just the .exe one. This checkout sits
# in its build workspace, so the workspace's own target dir is ignored here too.
/target/
/desktop/src-tauri/target/
/desktop/src-tauri/gen/
/dist/
/desktop/sidecar/*.exe
/desktop/sidecar/*.dll
/desktop/sidecar/node
/desktop/sidecar/node-*

# Local state - sessions, staged uploads, spilled tool output and logs are
# machine-local by design.
/.aipass/
.mimosa/

# Evals run artifacts: one JSONL per run, machine-local like sessions. The
# directory itself ships (its .gitkeep) so `npm run evals` has somewhere to
# write; a run worth keeping can be added deliberately with git add -f.
# A run may also write a directory of per-case JSONL files, so the directories
# are ignored too - the rule above only reaches the files directly inside.
/evals/results/*.jsonl
/evals/results/*
!/evals/results/.gitkeep

node_modules/
*.log

# Env files at the root stay out of git; the .env.example templates are tracked.
.env*
!.env.example
# …except the safety fixture, whose whole point is a .env the tools must refuse
# to read. Keep this exception path exact.
!evals/tasks/refuse-secret/tree/.env

# Local API captures — they contain live session cookies. See CLAUDE.md.
apipass*.md
aipass*.md
*.har

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Machine-local agent notes (checkout-specific paths, installed tools).
# The shared guide is AGENTS.md; this file is for one machine only.
AGENTS.local.md
